# 056 · A Codex CLI harness

**Status:** `READY` · **Version:** [v0.1.0](../roadmap.md#v010) · **Part:** Running campaigns

## What

Workers can run in the Codex CLI on Sign in with ChatGPT, as Claude Code runs on a Claude subscription.

## Why

Some owners will want OpenAI's own agent program.

## Done when

- [ ] A trial runs in the Codex CLI through the harness, on Sign in with ChatGPT, as trials run in Claude Code on a Claude subscription.
- [ ] Edit rig, `set_rig_model` and the rig's settings offer Codex as a harness for a ChatGPT sign-in, beside Pi and OpenCode.
- [ ] The planner and the model check run under it too, with the same isolation as the other harnesses, and the acceptance tests cover it with a stand-in.

## Decisions

- 2026-10-20, owner: a ChatGPT sign-in should also run workers in the Codex CLI, not only in Pi and OpenCode. The goal moves into v0.1.0.

## Open questions

None.

## Progress

- 2026-10-19: Goal written from the roadmap.
- 2026-10-20: Moved into v0.1.0 at the owner's word, after the owner signed in with ChatGPT on control.

